            <ArticleTitle>Primary breast chondrosarcoma: Imaging and pathological findings.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>138-140</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ejro.2017.11.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a 62 year-old woman who was admitted to our institute of radiological sciences for a breast mass developed in the last few months. The final diagnosis was primary breast chondrosarcoma and the surgical treatment performed, based on imaging and pathological findings, was the mastectomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
